frastructure plan receives NO T10 finding of ANY check class (including (g) teardown and (b2) endpoint-auth), not merely no prevent-destroy/blast-radius finding — or narrow the scope clause to state exactly which T10 checks it suppresses.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan goal: 'the durable-infrastructure and transient-experiment phases are disjoint'","AC3 only guards: 'does not receive a T10 prevent-destroy or blast-radius finding for that transient resource'","T10 rubric checks include (g) 'the resource is reproducible (as-code) with a clear teardown' and (b2) endpoint access contract for any service the plan STANDS UP — both can apply to a transient probe experiment","The proposed clause names 'creation, isolation, and teardown' as out of scope, implying ALL T10 checks should be carved out, but verification is scoped to only one check class"],"finding":"The scope clause claims to make the durable and transient phases disjoint, but the acceptance criteria and regression fixture only verify absence of a T10 prevent-destroy/blast-radius (check d) finding on the transient resource — while T10 also fires findings under check (g) 'clear teardown' and (b2) 'endpoint access contract'. A throwaway experiment that stands up a probe service or is torn down can still trip (g)/(b2), so the mechanism does not demonstrably achieve the stated disjointness for those check classes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9ddfa01615c1770e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (AC3) / Work: T10 scope clause","norm_id":"ncccd817f1eb0a35e","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["A throwaway experiment spins up a short-lived reachable probe service (triggers b2) or documents its teardown ambiguously (triggers g); T10 fires a finding despite the clause's disjointness promise"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Reword AC3 to 'does not receive ANY T10 finding for that transient resource (including prevent-destroy/blast-radius (d), teardown (g), and endpoint-auth (b2))' and add fixture assertions covering a transient probe that stands up a reachable service and one whose teardown is only informally described.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P7"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["destructive terms: destroy; no backup/dry-run/rollback nearby"],"finding":"Destructive/irreversible operation(s) with no stated safeguard.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4e1650fc06461e62","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"n4b1254c143290a68","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"State the safeguard (backup, dry-run, reversible migration, rollback) or justify the irreversibility explicitly (T4).","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an assertion (or cite the depended-on ticket via `[rebar:<C>]`) confirming that transient/throwaway de-risk infrastructure — creation, isolation, teardown — is covered by the sibling overlay this scope is partitioned toward, so the narrowing does not strand coverage.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T7","T9"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7437,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan asserts 'the durable-infrastructure and transient-experiment phases are disjoint' and 'T10 must not name T15 or reference ownership by another overlay'","Regression fixture asserts a torn-down transient resource receives NO T10 finding, intentionally removing that coverage from T10","No AC or step confirms the transient phase is still evaluated by the sibling overlay it is being partitioned toward"],"finding":"The plan narrows T10's scope to exclude transient de-risk infrastructure and forbids T10 from naming the owning overlay, but includes no acceptance criterion verifying that transient/throwaway infra (creation, isolation, teardown) remains covered by SOME overlay — risking a coverage hole where a plan's transient experiment gets no teardown/isolation scrutiny from any criterion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbc60922107724b56","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria / 'Keep the rubric independent' work bullet","norm_id":"naa491ab68ebc18c0","priority":0.2063,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["A plan whose only infra is a throwaway experiment with a missing teardown passes T10 (correctly out of scope) but is never checked by any overlay if the sibling's coverage was assumed but not verified"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_sta